<title>NETHERLANDS: ING plans modest U.S. placement.</title>
<headline>ING plans modest U.S. placement.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial services group ING said on Thursday it would combine its planned listing on the New York Stock Exchange with a small placement of existing shares and this would not dilute earnings per share.</p>
<p>&quot;At the moment preparations are being made to list ING shares in New York from the middle of June,&quot; the company said. &quot;It is intended to combine this with a placement of modest size of existing shares.&quot;  </p>
<p>&quot;This will cause no dilution of the earnings per share,&quot; the company added.</p>
<p>ING's earnings per share rose 18.8 percent in 1996 to 4.56 guilders per share.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
